  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target community for this meme is individuals who are aware of or engaged with discussions about religious intolerance, hypocrisy, and selective tolerance, particularly in the context of Islamophobia and religious extremism. The meme is designed to resonate with audiences familiar with critiques of religious double standards, and it implicitly targets or critiques communities that exhibit intolerance toward other religions while expecting tolerance for their own. The visual of the aggressive protest scene and the textual message are crafted to provoke reflection or criticism from those who recognize or have experienced such hypocrisy in religious or political discourse. The meme’s framing as a caricature of religious extremism and hypocrisy suggests it is aimed at an audience that understands or is concerned with issues of religious freedom, sectarianism, and social justice, particularly in relation to Muslim communities.",
